1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,157
Download the latest
release zip and extract it.

2
00:00:05,357 --> 00:00:08,800
Double-click "Install - Windows.bat".

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:15,300
PyTorch needs the Microsoft Visual C++
Runtime. If it's missing, press Enter.

4
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:19,657
Windows asks for
administrator permission once.

5
00:00:22,857 --> 00:00:29,657
The rest matches macOS: answer y to close
REAPER so its extensions can be installed.

6
00:00:29,857 --> 00:00:34,300
Python and the MIDI-GPT
backend take a few minutes.

7
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:41,300
The ReaImGui checksum warning is expected.

8
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:47,943
Answer y to open Sforzando's download
page, and keep the VST3 plug-in selected.

9
00:00:51,143 --> 00:00:55,014
Answer y to download
the Arachno SoundFont.

10
00:00:57,214 --> 00:01:02,586
Done. A "Start MIDI-GPT Server"
shortcut is now on your Desktop.
